From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 23:12:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] Draw through-point paths as the curve Pedro 3 follows

A path with through points is exported as Pedro's Paths.through(...), but
it was previewed with the Catmull-Rom chain that Pedro 2's
PathBuilder.curveThrough used. Pedro 3.0 removed curveThrough. Its
Paths.through fits a single Bezier that passes through pose i at
t = i / (n - 1) (BezierCurve.through, core 3.0.1). So the preview showed a
different route from the one the robot drives: on a four-point path the
two were up to 1.4 in apart, and Pedro's was about 4% longer.

lineCurvePoints now returns that Bezier's control points, found by solving
the Bernstein system that BezierCurve.through solves. Drawing, arc length,
animation, heading preview and code export all read the curve through
lineCurvePoints, so they all follow. The old code also fed about sixty
sampled spline points to getCurvePoint as if they were Bezier control
points, which smoothed the spline further; that goes away too.

The pen tool's live preview drew lineCurvePoints' output directly as a
polyline. It now samples the curve instead.

Checked against Pedro Pathing core 3.0.1 itself: the curves were compared
at 101 points each for five point sets (3 to 7 poses, uneven spacing, an
S-bend). The largest difference was 6.5e-11 in. svelte-check and the build
pass. ESLint warnings are unchanged. Prettier is clean on the changed
lines.
